## Menus

### GtkPopoverMenu with GtkMenuButton

Pass the menu through the menu button's `popover` prop. Inside `GtkPopoverMenu`, the
members are the short `Item`/`Section`/`Submenu` names. (If you instead build the menu
directly on `GtkMenuButton`, the members are `GtkMenuButton.MenuItem`/`.MenuSection`/`.MenuSubmenu`.)

```tsx
<GtkMenuButton
    iconName="open-menu-symbolic"
    popover={
        <GtkPopoverMenu>
            <GtkPopoverMenu.Section>
                <GtkPopoverMenu.Item id="new" label="New" onActivate={handleNew} accels="<Control>n" />
                <GtkPopoverMenu.Item id="open" label="Open" onActivate={handleOpen} />
            </GtkPopoverMenu.Section>
            <GtkPopoverMenu.Section>
                <GtkPopoverMenu.Submenu label="Export">
                    <GtkPopoverMenu.Item id="pdf" label="PDF" onActivate={exportPdf} />
                    <GtkPopoverMenu.Item id="csv" label="CSV" onActivate={exportCsv} />
                </GtkPopoverMenu.Submenu>
            </GtkPopoverMenu.Section>
            <GtkPopoverMenu.Section>
                <GtkPopoverMenu.Item id="quit" label="Quit" onActivate={quit} accels="<Control>q" />
            </GtkPopoverMenu.Section>
        </GtkPopoverMenu>
    }
/>
```

**Menu item props:** `id` (required), `label`, `onActivate`, `accels` (e.g., `"<Control>n"`)

